Two things this run learned that the ticket did not anticipate:

1) minimax-m2.5-230b is CURRENTLY DISABLED at AKI. Both shims refused it:
     /openai/v1  -> HTTP 500 {"error":{"message":"Endpoint disabled!","type":
                    "invalid_request_error","code":"request_failed"}}
     /anthropic  -> HTTP 529 {"type":"error","error":{"type":"overloaded_error",
                    "message":"Endpoint disabled!"}}
   Both tool captures were therefore taken on llama3-chat-8b. The 529 is a SECOND confirmed
   class of non-transient condition arriving as overloaded_error (k127 knew only the
   too-small-max_tokens one), so the POD warning k127 added is if anything understated.

2) THE HEADER CAPTURE CANNOT FEED t/12_rate_limit.t. AKI.IO sends no x-ratelimit-* and no
   anthropic-ratelimit-* headers on any of its three wires -- the captured header sets hold
   access-control-allow-origin, connection, content-length, content-type, date, server and
   nothing else. t/28 asserts that fact (has_rate_limit stays false after a real 200 driven
   through the shims' real parsers), which is the most those headers can prove. Replacing
   t/12's hand-written headers needs a capture from a provider that actually sends them.

